CON-14: book LID releases as a negative BMP removal instead of creating mass

SWMMEngine::bookWashoffLoads() ports surfqual_getWashoff()'s split of the
pre/post-LID volume difference, clamped at zero: when the LIDs release more
water than the subcatchment generates (vOut2 > vOut1), the surplus leaves
with the step's washoff concentration and no ledger term pays for it. Book
the signed difference, as the 5.3.0 patch does. Exported loads and
concentrations do not change.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-14_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
